By the end of the Triennium, "The Diary of a newly married poet" also appears
The first illustrative edition of The Diary of a newly married poet will be premiered at Saint Stephen's Church (New York), where Juan Ramón Jiménez married Zenobia in May 1916. The premiere is part of a series of programs titled Zenobia and Juan Ramón Triennium (2006-2008), organized by the Andaluus Regional Government’s Cultural Committee on the occasion of the Fiftyth Anniversary of the Nobel Prize.
In this way, the closing chord of Zenobia and Juan Ramón Triennium is a re-published edition of the above-mentioned work, the re-published edition of the International Congress held in New York, the memorial house of the Nobel laureate, and "Juan Ramón Jiménez: The Glorious Poplar" travelling exhibition "Juan Ramón Jiménez: The Glorious Poplar Tree".
The Cultural Committee of the Andaluus Regional Government has obtained a total of eight hundred specimens from the di diary published by Perdo Tabernero and illustrated by Jacobo Pérez-Enciso to promote the fame and work of one of the most versatile Andalusian poets.
