Those who speak in a dream
A couple of kids are talking at night.
I don't think of those who wake up and fully vigilant about what's going to happen to them this day, I'm talking to those who talk while they're asleep.
The phenomenon may seem frightening at the first time, but it's actually completely harmless.
This benevolent sleep disorder is called somniloquismus.
Quintly common, especially among children and adolescents.
I'm guessing many of them, they've been talking at night.
Concerning its frequency, it can be completely rhapsodic (e.g. it occurs only once with a high-registration disease), or it is more systematic (daily, every week or once a month), and usually the next day the child does not remember anything.
Its appearance cannot be traced back to a single trigger.
It is often coupled with other sleep disturbances, such as nightmares, nocturnation at night (enuresis nocturna) or sleepwalking.
As we have already mentioned, there may be an arrogant presence with a high fever or even a stressful state of excitement.
In any case, it's been little studied so far.
The intens intensity of speech is also very variable.
You may be quiet, relaxed, it may consist of incoherent words and grumbling, but, in contrast to all this, it may also occur in the form of yelling, weeping, or a lengthy speech.
If the phenomenon is very intense, it is advisable to observe the child and turn to a specialist. The examination can reveal whether there is a problem that provokes a lot of anxiety in the background and can therefore also offer a solution.
As we have already mentioned, it is a benevolent phenomenon, and consequently there is no cure for it, unless the sleep disorder is associated with some other manageable forms (such as insomnia or stressful situation).
But there's a few things we can do, here's a bunch of preventive measures:
Make sure the child stays calm before going to bed.
Choose reassiliating games and avoid watching your child’s fear-mongering or more aggressive TV shows or series.
Children professed to nervousness or are more difficult to relax are taught a few methods of relaxation to find inner peace of mind more easily.
This will help your child to have a more relaxed sleep.
Even if you begin to talk during your sleep, we will try to keep our peace of mind.
Don’t forget, it’s harmless for the child and they won’t remember anything the next day.
Beneficial advice
I don't wake the child.
Unnecessarily, because the child is not conscious, but would get me out of sleep.
Even though he talks, he's actually going to keep sleeping and relaxing.
Don’t forget, if there’s a lot of anxiety accompanies the phenomenon, it is advisable to turn to a specialist or to find out what provokes a high degree of anxiety from the child.
If he speaks clearly (this is the rarest case), don’t start asking them to find out anything.
It'd be superfluous anyway, because it's not so conscious when you're asleep to collect your thoughts.
On the other hand, you can only hear the speech, but you do not see the dreams associated with it, so be cautious about interpreting what you hear and possible conclusions.
Don’t ever tell your child to be questioned at night.
It's not even a joke.
This provokes a lot of anxiety.
The most important thing isn’t to worry, because it’s just a few minutes of harmless episode.
