Nicolas Sarkozy puts a detour into Brittany.
On Monday, the fishermen paralysed the traffic of several Breton and Norman harbours. Therefore, the President of the Republic decided to visit the port of Le Guilvinec in Finistare on Tuesday morning to meet the demonstrators.
The latter promised to welcome the president in a “constructive spirit” and expressed their hope that Sarkozy would “appropriate proposals”.
The presidential visit coincides with a "crisis committee" meeting set up by Breton fishermen with the aim of initiating action against an increase in the price of gasoline, as the oil price exceeded a record average of 1.14 euros per litre.
David Martinon, a spokesman for the President of the Republic, said: “The president will be negotiating with fishermen to find ways to help corporations regain their competitiveness and make it safer for seafarers to improve working conditions and salaries.”
