Remedies, fried juice is forbidden.
Beware of grapefruit, orange and almala.
These high-female criccre beverages, which are mainly popular in the summer, when enrolled together with certain life-saving medications, change their absorption by amplifying or diminishing their effect. This can also have serious health consequences.
David Bailey, a professor at the University of West Ontario in London, warned about the risk of co-approximatanial lesions and certain drugs. The professor announced at the 236th National Meeting of the American Chemical Society in Philadelia that a glass of grapefruit, orange or apple juice could reduce the absorption of certain life-saving drugs, thus preventing their beneficial effects and endangering the patient’s health.
Grapefruit juice had already been placed on the bench when it turned out to be able to increase the effects of antibiotic, antihistamine, anti-hythmetic, rhythm-reguling and nerve medication up to a toxic level.
Two years ago – Two years ago the Italian Pharmacy Institute itself published the news in its official gazette and warned physicians and patients to take seriously the risks associated with co-consumption, and to pay attention to what they drank when they received medicines such as Diazepam or Metadon.
GRAPEFRUIT – According to the researchers, orange and apple juice also contain substances that impede the effectiveness of the drugs.
A list of active substances whose absorption is impedied by grapefruit and other fruit juices could be listed.
Michele Carruba, a professor of pharmacology at the Department of Pharmacology at State University in Milan said: “Special discoveries of this kind are usually immediately reported to various national and international pharmaceutical institutes who, if necessary, make sure that they change the data contained in the information provided for in that medicine.
That’s why it’s always necessary to read the information about the medicine you intend to collect, and if something is incomprehensible, don’t let us influence ourselves, but we should definitely ask our doctor or pharmacist,” said the Ansa institute.
Paul Krugman receives Nobel Prize in Economics
U.S. Paul Krugman was awarded the Nobel Prize in Economics for analysing the territorial connections between commercial models and economic activity.
The 55-year-old neo-Cannesian Krugman at Princeton University and is a well-knowledvolved publicist for the New York Times.
Krugman is one of the greatest critics of the Bush administration’s economic and foreign policy measures.
A few months after the terrorist attack in September 2001, when Enron went bankrupt, Krugman predicted in an editorial published in the New York Times that the latter event would have even more crucial consequences for the history of the United States than the collapse of twin towers.
This instigation sparked a lot of controversy, it has been reproducing the economist on several occasions, but we now know that it was accurate.
“I’m surprised, and there’s been a little bit shocked by how quickly the public public interest has surpassed the outburst of Enron or Worldcom,” Krugman said at the end of 2002.
According to Lorenzo Bini Smaghi, a member of the Executive Committee of the European Central Bank, Krugman is a “crazy-precious economist”, but at the same time “disseminates in a rather “aggressive style of criticism of the Bush administration’s excessive liberalism.”
The "anti-Microsoft" package was also worth the third edition of Open Office
OpenOffice.org 3.0 is an open-end suite with personal productivity-enhancing open-denomiplity, targeting an ever-increasing number of layers as a free alternative in Microsoft Office, ranging from home-to-to-experienced users to public administration.
After working by SUN Microsystem for almost a year and carried out by voluntary developers, the new Open Office comes to the general public with a number of novelties: in addition to the greeting screen and a reconsidered, it also offers several important novelties, such as the compatibility with the Apple Mac OS X operational system, as well as the new ODF (Open Document Format) 1.2 format.
Particular attention has been paid to compatibility with the Office 2007 system, so Open Office can also open the newly extended Microsoft documents (.docx, .xlsx, .pptx).
It is also interesting to have the specific functions of a few modules, such as the one that makes it possible to reduce the size of PowerPoint presentations. This can be useful for sending files by e-mail. Another feature supports the import of PDF files into the graphical module, retaining the lateral layout.
You can also create “hybrid PDF” documents on this interface, which combines the typical Adobe format with spreadsheet or text editor items.
Sharing within applications has also undergone a number of improvements: the spreadsheet supports the joint use of workbooks, but it also prevents overwrite each other’s work. Each employee’s comments are marked in different colours, which helps easier recognization during the inspection phase.
Some companies are already working to ensure that some of OpenOffice’s features can also be accessed from the Internet (on the cloud), so the final version is likely to be presented in the next few weeks.
The Italian version can be downloaded from the following address: http://it.openoffice.org/download/3.0.0/download300.html
In addition to the usual Windows and Mac OS operative systems, the suite is also available for Linux.
On request, you can even receive the installation CD in your home or at your workplace.
In terms of proliferation of the home application, gratuity is probably the biggest attraction, but the Open Office suite is now also trying to get a ball in the business sector, as you can also count on a number of administrative and school projects.
There is no shortage of ideal education, consultancy and serroving services for small and medium-sized enterprises, which could open up new business prospects.
The Open Office consists of five core modules: Writer, Word-appropriate text editor; Calc, a spreadsheet in Excel-restricken dispensing; Impress, Powerpoint-like presentation; Dbase is the most well-known Access database manager; and finally Draw is the graphics module.
The 2008 goal is to achieve 5 million downloads, but if we take into account that with the release of the new version we are already at 3.600,000, this number is likely to be higher than expected.
